    "chunk_text": "previous governments. That is not rocket science; that is the key test we would apply when we look at this Budget. So, in that sense, I mentioned that we were hopeful and were actually looking forward to this Budget because there is an element within this Government, the predominant party, the JVP, being a leftist-oriented party, that it would not be too enamored by centre-right and right-wing economic policies, but there would be a tendency towards looking at the vulnerable, paying special attention to them, to protect them and their economies, making sure their economies would grow. That is a key element of leftist thinking. So, that was something we were actually looking forward to in this Government\u2019s Budget.\n\nAnd, that is true, that is exactly what we were expecting to see in this Budget. But honestly, Sir, there is nothing specific in this Budget for the North and the East, nothing specific to say that the North and the East, because of the war situation that existed for 30 years, is specifically vulnerable and must be protected."
