    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "5155a209c3767adecd624a00d6aba030",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2000,
    "chunk_text": "And, that is true, that is exactly what we were expecting to see in this Budget. But honestly, Sir, there is nothing specific in this Budget for the North and the East, nothing specific to say that the North and the East, because of the war situation that existed for 30 years, is specifically vulnerable and must be protected.\n\nAnother thing he specifically mentions is the allocation of Rs. 100 million to the Jaffna Public Library. Good, it is something that we welcome. But honestly, Sir, today, Rs. 100 million is nothing. You know that. I mean, a fairly wealthy person who tries to build a house in Colombo will not be able to complete it for Rs. 40 million\n\n1427 1428\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nor Rs. 50 million. So, what is Rs. 100 million for an entire library that was completely destroyed and still not restored to its original splendour? Therefore, when it comes to the details, there is a problem. We have repeatedly said this in previous Budgets. I have been a Member of Parliament since 2001 and at that time, we spoke in terms of needing a special provision for the North and the East because it was war-affected. Certainly, since I got re-elected in 2020, we have been saying that after 2009, the consecutive Governments should have declared the North and the East a war-affected area, brought in certain protectionist measures for, maybe, five years or ten years to ensure that the economies of the people who are vulnerable, who are literally 40 years behind the rest of the country are protected, strengthened and are allowed to grow, and once they are ready to compete with the rest of the country, then you can have an all-encompassing policy for the whole country. We have been saying that to the previous Governments, but, of course, none of those Governments listened. So, we were hoping that this Government, which is dominated by the JVP, a leftist party, would actually take that point, but they have not. And, as a result, there are serious concerns, Sir."
  },
