    "chunk_text": "or Rs. 50 million. So, what is Rs. 100 million for an entire library that was completely destroyed and still not restored to its original splendour? Therefore, when it comes to the details, there is a problem. We have repeatedly said this in previous Budgets. I have been a Member of Parliament since 2001 and at that time, we spoke in terms of needing a special provision for the North and the East because it was war-affected. Certainly, since I got re-elected in 2020, we have been saying that after 2009, the consecutive Governments should have declared the North and the East a war-affected area, brought in certain protectionist measures for, maybe, five years or ten years to ensure that the economies of the people who are vulnerable, who are literally 40 years behind the rest of the country are protected, strengthened and are allowed to grow, and once they are ready to compete with the rest of the country, then you can have an all-encompassing policy for the whole country. We have been saying that to the previous Governments, but, of course, none of those Governments listened. So, we were hoping that this Government, which is dominated by the JVP, a leftist party, would actually take that point, but they have not. And, as a result, there are serious concerns, Sir.\n\nAnd the Eastern Province\u2019s entire future, according to this Budget, depends on India. All are up in arms, Sir. So, even in that regard, we have no definite commitment because of your own policies, which, very clearly, might negatively impact on India.\n\n1429 1430\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca\u0dcf\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbd\u0dda \u0db8\u0dc0 \u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dc1\u0db4\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd2 25"
