    "chunk_size_bytes": 2265,
    "chunk_text": "And the Eastern Province\u2019s entire future, according to this Budget, depends on India. All are up in arms, Sir. So, even in that regard, we have no definite commitment because of your own policies, which, very clearly, might negatively impact on India.\n\n1429 1430\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc1\u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca\u0dcf\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbd\u0dda \u0db8\u0dc0 \u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dc1\u0db4\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd2 25\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc6\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. Member, you have only two more minutes. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0db4\u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bc7\u0bc0.\u0bc7\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0bc6\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) Hon. Deputy Speaker, please give me two extra minutes; two more minutes over the two minutes I have.\n\nAnd, there is nothing about any of that in this Budget. If you all do not tackle the Forest Department and the militarization in the North and the East, which the Government said it will - in the last three months, it has done nothing - then, this concept of agriculture and food security becomes a pipedream for people in the North and the East, Sir.\n\nThen, you talk about dairy production. Well and good, we will be supporting it to the highest. But, in Mayilathamadu and Madhavanai in the Eastern Province, over 30,000 acres of dairy lands allocated are today being forcibly and illegally confiscated by people from outside districts, preventing dairy production there. In the past, previous Governments had stood against the Tamil people on this question of dairy lands in Mayilathamadu and Madhavanai. There is not a word from this Government also with regard to that very vexed problem. Those people who are affected are protesting even today. It is the second longest protest this country has ever seen next to that of the families of the disappeared from the North and the East because their livelihoods are being destroyed.\n\nThere is not a word from the Government! So, without tackling this question of dairy production in the areas of Mayilathamadu and Madhavanai, Sir, this becomes meaningless for the people of the Eastern Province."
  },
