    "chunk_text": "Now, I am tired, Madam, of raising this repeatedly. Actually, there is a young gentleman who covers Parliamentary affairs and who has been good enough to cover my speeches. He made a comment. He said, \u201cSir, I\n\n301 302\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nThe speaker who spoke before me represents the Vanni Electoral District and the poor Hon. Member tried very hard to justify the allocations for defence and to play it down. Representing the Vanni, he also represents Mullaitivu; he being a Member of the Vanni means that Mullaitivu is a part of his Electorate. He should feel ashamed that he has to justify that 1:2 ratio!\n\nI honestly ask you, do you not feel claustrophobic? Do you not feel suffocated? Would you accept that in your areas? Would you?\n\nAnd, what else does the defence establishment do? The teachers of the defence establishment are teaching in preschools. I mentioned this even during the Budget Debate. The Defence establishment employs preschool teachers. The Ministry of Education employs preschool teachers for Rs. 6,000 while the defence establishment employs them for Rs. 30,000! In an area where you have had 35 years of war and where their economy is scraping the barrel, when you are given a choice between Rs. 6,000 and Rs. 30,000 or Rs. 40,000, which section of preschools would you want to get employed in? Are you not deliberately, by keeping that difference, militarizing education in the North and the East? What is the intention then? Therefore, is it a post-war feeling that you get when you listen to these figures? So, this has to change. Madam, I am tabling* two reports. One is a report by the Citizen Fact Check on this 1:2 ratio and the other is by Adayaalam Centre for Policy Research."
