    "chunk_size_bytes": 2208,
    "chunk_text": "And, what else does the defence establishment do? The teachers of the defence establishment are teaching in preschools. I mentioned this even during the Budget Debate. The Defence establishment employs preschool teachers. The Ministry of Education employs preschool teachers for Rs. 6,000 while the defence establishment employs them for Rs. 30,000! In an area where you have had 35 years of war and where their economy is scraping the barrel, when you are given a choice between Rs. 6,000 and Rs. 30,000 or Rs. 40,000, which section of preschools would you want to get employed in? Are you not deliberately, by keeping that difference, militarizing education in the North and the East? What is the intention then? Therefore, is it a post-war feeling that you get when you listen to these figures? So, this has to change. Madam, I am tabling* two reports. One is a report by the Citizen Fact Check on this 1:2 ratio and the other is by Adayaalam Centre for Policy Research.\n\nhave done is to begin to change this. Then, you would have had us believe that there is actually a chance of things happening differently. But, you have not done that; you have increased the Budgetary allocation instead. Despite the fact that we have been raising these issues at the Consultative Committee as well as on the Floor of this House, you have not done anything concrete to change that. On dividual instances - the Hon. Mano Ganesan brought up a few - we have brought this up, but you have not changed. Nothing has changed. So, this has to change, Madam. Without changing that, to simply tell us that you will get rid of racism is just hogwash; it means nothing.\n\nTherefore, we will be calling for a Division and will be voting against the Heads of both the Ministry of Defence and the Ministry of Public Security.\n\nThank you. \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dab \u0db1\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dba \u0da2\u0dba \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0bb3\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Chairperson) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0dba\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0dd2 \u0da2\u0dba\u0dc1\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dda\u0dbb \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf. \u0d94\u0db6\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0da9\u0dd2 12\u0dda \u0dda\u0dcf\u0d89\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dba \u0d89\u0dd0\u0db6\u0dd3 \u0dad\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db6\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf."
