    "chunk_text": "Sir, before I proceed, I must take this opportunity to extend my congratulations to the Hon. Leader of the Opposition on two remarkable achievements of his. Firstly, after a long time, he has managed to unite the entire Opposition to oppose the Budget, an accomplishment that no other Leader of the Opposition in the recent history has been able to achieve. Perhaps with just one exception, he has orchestrated a rare moment of consensus across all the Opposition Parties. Secondly, I must commend him on his eloquent and meticulously timed 45-minute speech, which compellingly outlined why this Budget is a failure. Perhaps, his speech was so impressive that the Hon. Leader of the House wished to make him the permanent Leader of the Opposition through constitutional means! Or is it, rather, that the Hon. Leader of the House desires to make his own party the permanent governing party through constitutional means and that is why he made these remarks, I wonder? But, Sir, this is not the first time in the history that a Government in power has dreamt of keeping the particular Opposition Leader in that role indefinitely, perhaps out of a desire to maintain their own grip on power permanently.\n\n457 458\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0dc4\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dc2\u0dab \u0db1\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb \u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 01\n\nLet me now say a few words about the daylight murder of Mr. Lasantha Wickrematunge. I appreciate that the Hon. President has finally acknowledged the bona fide of the Attorney-General\u2019s role in this case when the truth has been distorted on social media through misinformation and unprofessional speculations. However, I must also acknowledge that there are some highly knowledgeable and professional YouTubers - I do not want to mention the names as they will say I am trying to advertise them - who provide insight and credible analysis.\n\nNext, the long-forgotten murder of Dinesh Schaffter - we all have forgotten that - a crime shrouded in mystery"
