    "md5": "1d494de7d25df49e15f3cd14a7cef732",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1878,
    "chunk_text": "Let me now say a few words about the daylight murder of Mr. Lasantha Wickrematunge. I appreciate that the Hon. President has finally acknowledged the bona fide of the Attorney-General\u2019s role in this case when the truth has been distorted on social media through misinformation and unprofessional speculations. However, I must also acknowledge that there are some highly knowledgeable and professional YouTubers - I do not want to mention the names as they will say I am trying to advertise them - who provide insight and credible analysis.\n\nNext, the long-forgotten murder of Dinesh Schaffter - we all have forgotten that - a crime shrouded in mystery\n\nThen, the infamous Central Bank Bond scam. I addressed that yesterday, but let me reiterate it. The authorities must proceed with the trial in absentia - I know the Minister of Justice knows about it - under the provisions of the Code of Criminal Procedure. We cannot wait till Arjuna Mahendran is sent here; it must start off in absentia. Extraditing a suspect is an unachievable task in the current state of the justice system because we are in a hell of a mess today. This has been deliberately undermined. However, I am confident that once the suspect is convicted, the Singaporean authorities would find it difficult to refuse his extradition.\n\nAnd then, the recent series of killings clearly point to organized crimes. It seems that the people behind these murders are deciding who should be arrested and who should not be. In the murder of \"Ganemulle Sanjeewa\", look at how easily the shooter was arrested. Yet, the woman who coordinated the attack, who is in the centre of all the key players in that Hollywood-style shooting, remains untouched. Is she, perhaps, the Sarah Jasmin of this killing? And, we know what happened to Sarah Jasmin. Sir, I am wondering whether the same thing would happen to this lady also."
  },
