    "chunk_size_bytes": 2327,
    "chunk_text": "And then, the recent series of killings clearly point to organized crimes. It seems that the people behind these murders are deciding who should be arrested and who should not be. In the murder of \"Ganemulle Sanjeewa\", look at how easily the shooter was arrested. Yet, the woman who coordinated the attack, who is in the centre of all the key players in that Hollywood-style shooting, remains untouched. Is she, perhaps, the Sarah Jasmin of this killing? And, we know what happened to Sarah Jasmin. Sir, I am wondering whether the same thing would happen to this lady also.\n\n459 460\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0dca \u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc0\n\nthink this Government is going to take my service. I am not even called upon to serve as a member of the Panel of Chairs, leave alone taking my service for the State. That does not matter. But, when I am called upon to defend the country and its integrity, I wondered how I should respond to the President\u2019s statement. So, leave alone the public, Hon. Minister of Justice, the President himself has lost confidence in the system of administration of justice! Please take a note of that fact. He did not spare anybody; police officers, officers of the forces, judicial officers and lawyers are being accused of creating a \u0d85\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dca\u200d \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dba\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca. That is a very serious matter. My only consolation is that the Hon. Minister of Justice, being a senior lawyer - though you are not a President\u2019s Counsel, I feel you are entitled it to be conferred on with your experience, both in the official and unofficial bar - would be able to put things into proper perspective and dispel any misconceptions about our profession.\n\nSir, I want to conclude because I have a very limited time, following the new trend set by the Hon. Wasantha Samarasinghe. He wound up his speech with the words of a song.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0db0\u0dc4\u0daf\u0dc0\u0dc1\u0dad\u0dca \u0d9c\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dba\u0dcf\u0db0 \u0db1\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dca \u0dc4\u0db3\u0dd4\u0dca \u0dc0\u0db1, \u0da0\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb \u0dc0\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0d82\u0dc4 \u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dba\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0d9c\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dc1\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dca \u0d89\u0dca \u0db1\u0dc0\u0dcf.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da0\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dbb \u0dd9\u0db8\u0dca\u0db4\u0dad\u0dca \u0daf\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dd9\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0bbe\u0bae\u0bb0 \u0b9a\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0b9a\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Chamara Sampath Dasanayake) \u0da0\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dca\u0db4\u0dad\u0dca \u0dc1\u0db1\u0ddc\u0dc1\u0dc0\u0dba\u0dd2 \u0dc1\u0dca ."
