    "md5": "a9d2f9c49001fafd93c0c19a6c9779b1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1998,
    "chunk_text": "Attorney-General\u2019s Department to prosecute those officials, and it is the view of all those professional lawyers, counsels who have been appearing for similar cases, that there is a major conflict of interest, where the Attorney-General\u2019s Department, that is the primary lawyer for the State, for the armed forces, is asked to go against the State in cases such as this. So, very obviously, there is a conflict of interest and in that case, the whole credibility of these proceedings comes into question.\n\nThe second point I wish to raise, Madam, is the question of mass graves. In the North and the East, there had been instances where mass graves had been found. One was found in the Sathosa Building in Kokkuthoduvai and another in Mannar, just beyond the bridge, the causeway. Then, as of two weeks ago, in the cemetery in Chemmani, Jaffna, there had been skeletal remains found.\n\nIn fact, I personally went and had a look. At that time when I went and had a look, the police had not taken any action; the Magistrate had not been informed. It was one of our party members, who also happens to be in the committee of the cemetery, whom I asked to make a formal complaint to the police. Thereafter, the Magistrate got involved and the matter is now being looked into. But, with the question of mass graves, Hon. Minister, there is no protocol. To my knowledge, there is no clear protocol to handle mass graves. As a result, there is a severe shortage of funds and it is almost always the case where the Government Agent is asked to get involved. The OMP, I think, has a little bit of funds, but nowhere close to the sort of resources required for the work that has to be done by the Department of Government Analyst and the courts to have this matter looked into as a matter of urgency. As a result, because of things getting dragged on, both in Kokkuthoduvai in Mannar and now, in Chemmani, Jaffna, evidence can get destroyed or tampered with. These are questions of mass graves and\n\n501 502"
  },
