    "chunk_text": "So, it is in that context I am raising these issues and as far as I am concerned, the evidence must be protected. You must, at least, try and protect that evidence. With regard to how these issues are to be looked at, you all have been suggesting an internal mechanism. My view is that that is just a non-starter. So, at the very least, if you could ensure that this evidence is protected and is recorded in a credible manner, I think that is the best you could do under these circumstances. I, for one, am not going to ask you to actually investigate it. I wish Sri Lanka was different; I wish we, as victims, could have said that we have credibility, that we look upon the system with credibility, but we do not. Nothing has happened so far to suggest that that situation will change. So, my request to you is that you intervene and ensure that adequate funds, adequate resources are given to protect the evidence in the mass graves so that at one point, when there is some agreement with regard to how to proceed on the question of accountability with the victims, then, this evidence could properly be used.\n\nHon. Minister, it is in this backdrop that several senior officials from the Attorney-General\u2019s Department are preferred to be appointed to the apex courts. Currently - correct me if I am wrong - in the Supreme Court, out of the 17 judges, except for four, all the others are from the Attorney-General\u2019s Department."
