    "description": "Hansard of March 01, 2025",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1741955797040395.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-03-01-2025-03-01-0178",
    "chunk_index": 178,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "f69e4c8452e2416657a94b778352c8da",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1954,
    "chunk_text": "Another suggestion I would like to make is, empowering judges to impose realistic costs. As you know, at the moment, judges in our legal system do not seem to award high costs and as a result, we see a lot of frivolous actions being instituted against people. Therefore, if we have some sort of guidelines in place by updating the relevant gazettes, the judges could award higher costs, which would also help speed up the process.\n\nI would request the Hon. Minister to help us in this process as the lawyers are willing to use their own funds and contribute towards the building. However, the only problem is that the cost per lawyer is Rs. 3.5 million and they would like to be given a period of five to ten years to pay that amount. As you know, these contributions will be made mostly by new, young lawyers and Rs. 3.5 million is a large sum of money, especially for those in the outstation Bars. So, I would request you to consider giving at least a period of five to ten years for those lawyers to pay that amount back to the Government.\n\n509 510\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2 \u0da0\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dca \u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dab\u0dd3 \u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0d87\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd \u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba ]\n\n2025 \u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 01\n\nMadam, let me raise just one more matter. Usually, commercial matters exceeding Rs. 50 million are referred to the Commercial High Court, Colombo. Once again, I would request the Hon. Minister - I think you would definitely agree with me, as we are both members of the Honourable Society of Lincoln\u2019s Inn - that a part-time Commercial High Court be instituted to hear commercial matters exceeding Rs. 50 million. Then, it would be easier for the lawyers in Kandy since, otherwise, they would have to travel all the way to Colombo for the hearings of those cases.\n\nFinally, I would like to wish the Hon. Harshana Nanayakkara all the best! We would also like to extend our assistance to solve any legal issues which we may have to face in Sri Lanka.\n\nThank you."
  },
