    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "8796907c68cb853015844e9905a32545",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1838,
    "chunk_text": "One of the most pressing concerns is the process of promoting career judges, particularly their appointments to the Court of Appeal and to the Supreme Court. While it is customary for promotions to follow the principle of seniority, it is not uncommon, Hon. Minister, for senior judges to be overlooked. Yet, in many instances, the\n\n533 534\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0dc1\u0d9a\u0dca.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0d85\u0dc3\u0dca\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 01\n\nFurthermore, judges must be protected from unwarranted attacks in Parliament. In the recent past, we have seen Privileges being utilized in the House to attack various persons including judges. So, if any Member wants to attack another, not only judges, using Privileges, he has to be cautious. If you use Privileges to attack somebody, you are a coward because you are taking protection of your Privileges in Parliament.\n\nThe independence of the Judiciary is a cornerstone of our democracy and it must remain untarnished and free from undue attack. In today\u2019s era of social media, attacks on judges made on the Floor of the House can have far-reaching consequences, eroding public confidence in the Judiciary. So, it is not only against a person, but also against the system. Judges, by virtue of their role, cannot respond to the allegations; you make statements against a person who is muted. I say that it is a cowardly act. I am not suggesting that Parliament should avoid addressing concerns regarding judges, they should. But, our Standing Orders should be amended to ensure that such matters are first examined through a structured process. Hon. Minister of justice, if you would look at the Standing Orders, you would notice that especially with regard to judges, there is a process to be followed before a Member comes to Parliament and makes various statements attacking them."
