    "chunk_text": "Madam, if you take the recent laws which were brought in with regard to remand prisoners, there was an Amendment brought in 2024, under which the period they were in remand was considered a part of their sentence and they could be released consequent to that; if they served a particular period in remand, that is also taken into consideration.\n\nto be sent to do community service. There is a law, I believe, brought in the 90s. So, if those provisions can be invoked, I am sure it will ease the congestion in prisons.\n\nThen, I saw that over 30 per cent of the Budget has been allocated for prison and prison reforms.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, your time is up. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0db1\u0dcf\u0db0\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dd2\u0dc3 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0da5 \u0dc6\u0dba\u0dd2\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dc4\u0dd4\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dad\u0dcf\u0db4\u0dcf \u0db8\u0dd9\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0ba9\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baa\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0bc8\u0bbf \u0b95\u0baa\u0bb8\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bc1\u0bb8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bbe) (The Hon. Faiszer Musthapha, PC) Please give me one minute, Madam.\n\nIf you could shift the Magazine Prison, those resources could be used. You do not have to have prisons in urban areas. If you could create more prisons in other areas, the facilities could be given. If you take the conditions of the prisoners today, they do not have even the basic needs such as water and sanitation. Some prisoners, when they are locked up, keep a bottle in the cell in night because they cannot go to the toilet.\n\nI respectfully urge you, Hon. Minister of Justice, to look at the suggestions I made, which, I am sure, would strengthen the legal process in this country. You are trying to create a better society and prisoners are sent to prisons so that they would reform. But, unfortunately, what is happening today is the converse. So, if you could give priority to continuous legal education and training them in various skills, we could make a great change with regard to how the prisoners are dealt with.\n\nMadam, I thank you once again for giving me the opportunity of speaking a few words."
  },
