    "md5": "78fcd7d654dca27f0084f109daf598ce",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1672,
    "chunk_text": "That is the biggest problem. We say, justice delayed is justice denied. And, you know very well that there are the number of cases filed and the number of cases disposed of in a particular year. I think the Minister of Justice knows about it. The numbers must match. When they do not match, we will end up having a big backlog of cases. For example, in Singapore, they always match. Sometimes, their system is more efficient that there are more cases disposed of than the cases filed in a particular year.\n\n\"Members of Parliament often make pronouncements targeting these institutions, possibly to appease their electorate.\"\n\n\"This is a dangerous trend that further erodes credibility and weakens the justice system.\n\nTherefore, I propose the establishment of a Select Committee on the Administration of Justice with the objective of preparing a report for implementation on the following matters, among others that may be included later:\n\n1. Expediting Pending Criminal Cases -.......\"\n\nThere is a huge backlog.\n\n\"..... Exploring ways to accelerate the resolution of pending criminal cases within the framework of the Law.\"\n\nThat should be done within the existing Code of Criminal Procedure.\n\n\" 2. Fast-Tracking Investigations and Indictments - Ensuring prompt investigation and filing of indictments in major crimes that have shocked the public, such as the murder of Dinesh Shafter, the masterminds behind the Easter Sunday attacks and the recent underworld-related shootings.\"\n\nSir, I mentioned this earlier also, that it has been ten years since the Central Bank Bond scam happened; the murder of Dinesh Shafter was in 2022 and the Easter Sunday attacks was in 2019."
