    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c7f42241d16d75632bf348d0267e957e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1886,
    "chunk_text": "\" 2. Fast-Tracking Investigations and Indictments - Ensuring prompt investigation and filing of indictments in major crimes that have shocked the public, such as the murder of Dinesh Shafter, the masterminds behind the Easter Sunday attacks and the recent underworld-related shootings.\"\n\nSir, I mentioned this earlier also, that it has been ten years since the Central Bank Bond scam happened; the murder of Dinesh Shafter was in 2022 and the Easter Sunday attacks was in 2019.\n\n\" 4. Engaging Specialists - Facilitating the engagement of specialists, either through hiring or obtaining the honorary services, to assist in investigations and the preparation of charge sheets and indictments. \"\n\nI think there are so many people who are willing to give their services on honorary basis to this Government, especially to assist investigations and the preparation of charge sheets and indictments. We have to have it.\n\n573 574\n\n2025 \u0dcf\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8 01\n\nOtherwise, the Attorney-General would not be able to cope up with the backlog they are having.\n\n\"5. Establishing Provincial-Level Prosecuting Offices - Integrating the Police Legal Division and the officer of the Attorney-General's Department at the provincial level.\"\n\nAdditionally, you can provide ad-hoc financial provisions to recruit temporary State Counsels at the senior level in the provinces. You can retain retired High Court Judges and some retired State Counsels who will work at the provincial level so that they need not send the documents - advice files - to the Attorney-General. There is a huge number of advice files pending in the Attorney-General's Department.\n\nSo, what I am saying is, let us have a Select Committee crucially to restore public confidence in the justice system, ensuring its efficiency and effective function. I urge this House to consider this Motion seriously and appoint a Select Committee."
  },
